  "challenge": "The negative quantity and negative total are mutually consistent with a net credit (return of 5 WidgetA at the exact reference price $250 plus purchase of 2 WidgetB at the exact reference price $500 yields -1250 + 1000 = -250, which matches stated total exactly); AR-002 is then just a wrong subtotal field, not broken economics. Policy for AR-006 itself frames the remedy as treating a negative total as a credit memo rather than an unpayable invoice, and both items are active catalog components—so this reads as a mis-typed credit memo, not garbage. Empty vendor (VN-005) still blocks straight payment, but the coherent credit-memo reading means the right move is escalation for vendor identification and reclassification, not flat REJECT.",
